:markdown
  The *Prince of Postcards* paintings are an ongoing series. They
  are an English take on the huge, industrial scale, quintessentially
  American "joke" paintings made by Richard Prince.

  After [work which removed text to change the meaning of an existing
  object](/series/ill_tell_you_whats_a_great_album), I chose to reverse
  the idea, using only the text from saucy seaside postcards &mdash; the
  most stereotypically English joke I could imagine.  Without the image,
  the innuendo is lost, and the message is changed.

  Each painting is six by four inches, the dimensions of a British
  postcard.

